#### Downstream complete charged specification and Thomson map

The primitive gate ends with `kappa_record`. It does not output
`kappa_Thomson`, `e`, or alpha.

A distinct sealed object `Q_spec` must define the complete physical charged
transition amplitude. It must contain, with no measured alpha:

```text
the charged boundary carrier and unit action-character current;
all charged source sectors and their statistics;
the gauge, constraint, ghost if required, and public edge sectors;
the preparation and durable-record projectors;
the microscopic measure and regulator;
the regulator-removal and locality theorem;
the Ward identity and transverse physical quotient;
the derived charged spectrum and every threshold entering the response;
decoupling and matching rules;
and the zero-momentum Thomson prescription.
```

Measured masses or threshold locations may be used for a phenomenological
consistency calculation, but not for a first-principles alpha claim. For the
end-to-end claim sought here, every load-bearing threshold must be derived
from the same sealed theory or proved irrelevant to the final coefficient.

The normalized physical amplitude is

```text
Z_Q[A]/Z_Q[0],
Gamma_Q[A]=-i Log(Z_Q[A]/Z_Q[0]),
```

with the logarithm branch fixed continuously at `A=0`. The complete
transverse quadratic response is defined by

```text
Gamma_Q^(2)[A]
 = (1/2) integral d^4q/(2 pi)^4
   A_mu(-q) (q^2 eta^(mu nu)-q^mu q^nu)
   kappa_Q(q^2) A_nu(q).
```

Pass requires the Ward identity, gauge-parameter independence on the
physical quotient, regulator independence, threshold matching, and a finite
path-independent limit

```text
kappa_Thomson=lim_(q^2->0) kappa_Q(q^2).
```

The old family `Gamma_c=-c log|A|` is resolved only here: `Gamma_Q` is
computed from the physical amplitude itself. Replacing `Z_Q/Z_Q[0]` by its
`c`th power changes that amplitude and describes `c` copies or a different
theory. If a multiplicity remains, it must be derived from `Q_spec`; it may
not be selected by the desired coupling.

The primitive `kappa_record` may constrain or appear inside this
construction, but equality

```text
kappa_record=kappa_Thomson
```

is not assumed. It must follow from the complete amplitude or fail.
Determinants, heat kernels, Wick rotations, regulators, and counterterms are
forbidden as primitive selectors but may appear here only when derived by
`Q_spec`. Regulator removal must leave no independently adjustable finite
`F^2` counterterm; otherwise the absolute coupling is not predicted.

Only after `kappa_Thomson` is derived may the unit-character convention be
applied:

```text
S_EM=-(kappa_Thomson/4) integral d^4x F_(mu nu)F^(mu nu),
kappa_Thomson=1/e^2,
alpha(0)=e^2/(4 pi)=1/(4 pi kappa_Thomson).
```

The canonical phase-space/Legendre construction is then an independent
consistency check on the resulting Lorentzian action. It cannot supply a
missing normalization.